      "pronunciationText": "Last time, we found our mixture was seventy percent salt, by separating it and weighing the parts. But salt itself is a compound. Its sodium and chlorine are bonded in a fixed ratio, one sodium for every chlorine, so no filter can split them. Here's the surprise. Because that ratio is fixed, you don't need to split it. The formula alone tells you what percentage of the mass comes from each element. We'll build the method on carbon dioxide, and then you'll use it on salt yourself.",
